# PRD: BabaSwift AppStore - Custom Android App Store Platform

**Version:** 1.0  
**Date:** May 22, 2026  
**Author:** BabaStore  
**Status:** Complete for Development

## 1. Product Overview

A full-featured web-based Android app store clone with Play Store-like UX. Users can browse, search, download APKs. Developers can upload and manage apps. Admins have full control. 

**Core Value Proposition:**  
- Zero platform fees on downloads (or configurable).  
- Direct APK hosting on Cloudflare R2 (cheap + fast).  
- Supabase backend + Resend auth.  
- Modern dark glassmorphism UI inspired by Vercel.

**Target Users:**
- End Users (download apps)
- Developers (upload & monetize)
- Admins (moderate platform)

## 2. Tech Stack (Fixed)

- **Frontend:** Next.js 15 (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- **UI Theme:** Vercel-inspired dark theme + heavy glassmorphism (transparent frosted cards, blur effects, neon accents)
- **Backend:** Supabase (PostgreSQL, Auth, Storage proxy if needed)
- **File Storage:** Cloudflare R2 (for APKs + screenshots + icons)
- **Auth:** Email + Password + Resend (email confirmation, password reset)
- **Emails:** Resend
- **Other:** Zod validation, TanStack Query, React Hook Form, Framer Motion

## 3. User Roles & Dashboards

### 3.1 User Dashboard (Play Store style)
- Home feed (Featured, Trending, Categories, New Releases)
- Search with filters (category, rating, size, updated date)
- App detail page (screenshots carousel, description, version history, reviews, "Install" button)
- My Apps (installed/downloaded history)
- Wishlist
- Profile & Settings
- Download manager (progress + resume support via R2 signed URLs)

### 3.2 Developer Dashboard
- My Apps list
- Upload new APK (multi-version support)
- App metadata editor (name, description, category, tags, privacy policy URL, etc.)
- Screenshots & icon uploader
- Analytics (downloads, installs, ratings)
- Revenue reports (if monetization added later)
- Version management & changelog
- Publish / Unpublish toggle

### 3.3 Admin Dashboard
- All Apps moderation (approve/reject/flag)
- Users management (ban, verify)
- Developers management
- Categories management
- Global announcements
- Analytics dashboard (total downloads, active users, storage usage)
- Reports & logs
- R2 storage usage monitor

## 4. Key Features & Flows (Phased)

### Phase 1: Foundation & Auth (Week 1-2)
- Supabase project setup (DB schema, RLS policies)
- Resend integration for:
  - Email confirmation
  - Password reset
  - Welcome emails
- Auth pages: Login, Register, Forgot Password (glassmorphism forms)
- Protected routes middleware
- Role-based access (user/developer/admin) – stored in Supabase profiles table
- Design system setup (design.md equivalent – dark theme, glass cards, hover effects, mobile responsive)

**Database Tables (initial):**
- profiles (id, role, email, username, avatar)
- apps (id, developer_id, name, package_name, version, apk_url, icon_url, status: draft/published/rejected)
- app_versions
- app_screenshots
- categories
- reviews
- downloads (tracking)

### Phase 2: Core App Browsing & Download (Week 2-3)
- Public homepage mimicking Play Store (hero banner, tabs: For You, Top Charts, Categories)
- Infinite scroll + search + filters
- App detail page with:
  - Glassmorphism info cards
  - Image carousel (screenshots)
  - "Install" button → direct R2 signed URL download
- Download logging
- Responsive mobile-first UI (PWA ready)

### Phase 3: Developer Features (Week 3-4)
- Developer portal with sidebar navigation
- APK upload (large file support via R2 direct upload or presigned URLs)
- Metadata form with rich text editor (description)
- Auto package name validation
- Versioning system
- Preview before publish

### Phase 4: Admin Panel & Moderation (Week 4-5)
- Separate /admin route (role guard)
- Review queue for new apps
- Bulk actions
- Basic analytics (use Supabase + simple charts with Recharts)

### Phase 5: Polish, Reviews & Analytics (Week 5-6)
- User reviews & ratings system
- Rating aggregation
- Developer response to reviews
- Basic search ranking
- Wishlist
- "Similar apps" section
- Dark glassmorphism perfection (blur-3xl, border opacity, etc.)

### Phase 6: Advanced & Launch (Week 6-7)
- PWA installation support
- Download verification (hash check optional)
- Rate limiting & abuse prevention
- SEO (Next.js metadata, sitemaps)
- Analytics integration (PostHog or Umami)
- Error monitoring (Sentry)
- Final testing & deployment

## 5. UI/UX Requirements (design.md style)

- **Theme:** Pure dark (#0A0A0A base) + glassmorphism (`backdrop-blur-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10`)
- Vercel-like typography (Inter/Satoshi)
- Neon accents on primary actions (purple/blue)
- Smooth animations (Framer Motion)
- Play Store layout:
  - Top nav with search + avatar
  - Bottom nav on mobile
  - Card grid for apps
- All pages fully responsive

## 6. Non-Functional Requirements
- Fast loading (R2 + Next.js edge)
- Secure downloads (time-limited signed URLs)
- RLS on Supabase (developers can only edit own apps)
- File size limits (configurable, e.g., 200MB per APK)
- Virus scanning recommendation (later via API)
- GDPR ready (data export, delete)

## 7. Future Phases (Post MVP)
- In-app purchases / subscriptions for developers
- Paid apps + revenue share
- Comments system
- Push notifications (web)
- iOS IPA support
- API for third-party clients
- AI app recommendations

## 8. Acceptance Criteria
- All dashboards functional per role
- Successful APK upload → public download works
- Glassmorphism UI matches reference screenshots (Vercel + Play Store hybrid)
- Email flows tested
- Mobile experience excellent

**Deployment:**
- Vercel (frontend)
- Supabase
- Cloudflare R2 + custom domain

---

**Instructions for Agent:**  
Build strictly in the phases above. Start with Phase 1. After each phase, commit to Git with clear messages. Use shadcn/ui components heavily. Ask Baba Swift if any clarification needed.

End of PRD.